WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.000
Vehicle Lab connects ideation, prototyping, inspection, evolution, physics and assembly planning.

2
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:22.000
The baseline makes assumptions visible. Geometry helps ask better questions before parts are selected.

3
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:35.000
This is the actual RC25 CAD export. Separating the parts is an inspection animation, not a proven assembly path.

4
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Native mesh geometry exposes the chain, bearing and frame detail. Detail alone does not close mechanical fit.

5
00:00:48.000 --> 00:01:01.000
Design evolution is a revision history. No evolutionary optimizer or physical prototype campaign is claimed.

6
00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:16.000
A real saved solver run, replayed at 1× during the motion segment. The failed obstacle test stays visible.

7
00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:29.000
Assembly planning connects part identity to the next experiment. Physical verification is the next engineering step.

8
00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:36.000
Vehicle Lab · an experimental pipeline from design intent to inspectable evidence.
